0 61 148 [
[(A random walk is a special case of a Markov chain, in which)]
[(the states are integers and the transitions add or subtract)]
[(a small amount from the previous state to get a new one.)]
[(Here the [f] holds the state. When it gets a bang, the)]
[(previous state is added to a random number \050from 1 to 4\051)]
[(multiplied by a random sign \050-1 or 1\051. The new value is then)]
[(coerced into the range \050from 0 to 100\051.)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
